From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/24] mfd: exynos-lpass: keep LPASS active while its UART is
 enabled

The UART sub-block has no runtime PM of its own. Once LPASS runtime-
suspends right after probe, exynos_lpass_disable() clears
SFR_LPASS_INTR_CPU_MASK, which masks the UART interrupt: a serial device
behind it never completes a transmission (hci_bcm: "command 0x0c03 tx
timeout"). The vendor kernel keeps the block on for its UART ("audio
uart always on").

Take a runtime PM reference in probe when an enabled
samsung,exynos5433-uart child exists, and drop it in the remove action.

Checked on the SM-T715 (Bluetooth on UART3): CTS rises as soon as BT_EN
is set, the controller answers HCI_Reset and loads its patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/mfd/exynos-lpass.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/exynos-lpass.c b/drivers/mfd/exynos-lpass.c
index 8b5fed476..1005c6845 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/exynos-lpass.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/exynos-lpass.c
@@ -52,6 +52,8 @@ struct exynos_lpass {
 	/* pointer to the LPASS TOP regmap */
 	struct regmap *top;
 	struct clk *sfr0_clk;
+	/* runtime PM reference held for the UART sub-block */
+	bool uart_ref;
 };
 
 static void exynos_lpass_core_sw_reset(struct exynos_lpass *lpass, int mask)
@@ -109,6 +111,8 @@ static void exynos_lpass_disable_lpass(void *data)
 	struct platform_device *pdev = data;
 	struct exynos_lpass *lpass = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
+	if (lpass->uart_ref)
+		pm_runtime_put_noidle(&pdev->dev);
 	pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
 	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(&pdev->dev))
 		exynos_lpass_disable(lpass);
@@ -118,6 +122,7 @@ static int exynos_lpass_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	struct exynos_lpass *lpass;
+	struct device_node *uart;
 	void __iomem *base_top;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -142,6 +147,21 @@ static int exynos_lpass_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, lpass);
 	pm_runtime_set_active(dev);
+
+	/*
+	 * The UART sub-block has no runtime PM of its own, and suspending
+	 * LPASS clears SFR_LPASS_INTR_CPU_MASK, which masks the UART
+	 * interrupt: a serial device behind it (e.g. Bluetooth) then sees
+	 * every transmission time out.  Keep the block active while an
+	 * enabled UART child exists, as the vendor kernel does.
+	 */
+	uart = of_get_compatible_child(dev->of_node, "samsung,exynos5433-uart");
+	if (uart && of_device_is_available(uart)) {
+		pm_runtime_get_noresume(dev);
+		lpass->uart_ref = true;
+	}
+	of_node_put(uart);
+
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
 	exynos_lpass_enable(lpass);
 
